1. A method of fabricating a magnetic random access memory (MRAM) device, the method comprising:

forming a magnetic tunnel junction (MTJ) stack over a substrate, the MTJ stack comprising a reference magnetic layer, a tunnel barrier layer, and a free magnetic layer;

performing a first etching process on the MTJ stack to define a patterned MTJ stack having sidewalls, wherein the first etching process causes metallic redeposition material to be present on the sidewalls of the patterned MTJ stack;

forming a sacrificial dielectric material over the patterned MTJ stack such that the sacrificial dielectric material covers the metallic redeposition material on the sidewalls;

removing at least a portion of the metallic redeposition material from the sidewalls after forming the sacrificial dielectric material; and

performing a second etching process on the patterned MTJ stack after removing the at least a portion of the metallic redeposition material, the second etching process trimming the patterned MTJ stack to reduce a lateral width of the patterned MTJ stack.
